pert Roadmap by Sprints
// stress: span — sprint-counted cells; an FF edge label over an edge that runs along the top row (#2117)
time-unit s
sprint-length 2w
sprint-number 12

# Three-month plan, sprint-counted. Cells render as `S<n>` (e.g. S12,
# S15) instead of dates or numeric offsets, so this chart can sit
# alongside a Jira/Linear cycle view without translation.
#
# `time-unit s` auto-activates sprint mode; `sprint-length 2w` makes
# each sprint two weeks (the analyzer's underlying canonical-day math
# uses 14d per sprint instead of the un-authored 14d fallback —
# semantically the same here, but explicit).
# `sprint-number 12` labels the starting sprint as S12.

discovery 1 2 3
prototype 2 3 4
build core 3 4 5
beta release 1 1 1
gather feedback 1 2 3
ga launch 1 1 2

discovery
  -> prototype
prototype
  -> build core
build core
  -> beta release
beta release
  -SS+1s-> gather feedback
gather feedback
  -> ga launch
build core
  -FF-> ga launch
